1
00:00:05,068 --> 00:00:10,490
RAPID INCREASE
IN FOREIGN TOURISTS IN JAPAN!

2
00:01:01,791 --> 00:01:05,461
Foreign tourists have it so good,
living in luxury.

3
00:01:05,545 --> 00:01:07,422
We Japanese

4
00:01:07,505 --> 00:01:11,217
don't have the time or the money
to be talking about vacations!

5
00:01:13,469 --> 00:01:15,972
When would you like to make
your next appointment?

6
00:01:16,055 --> 00:01:17,265
Let's see…

7
00:01:17,348 --> 00:01:20,185
How about next Wednesday at 4:00 p.m.?

8
00:01:20,268 --> 00:01:21,644
Yes, that's available.

9
00:01:21,728 --> 00:01:23,396
So, on the 22nd--

10
00:01:23,479 --> 00:01:25,773
Wait, no.
I have a nail appointment that day.

11
00:01:25,857 --> 00:01:28,067
Would you like to choose another day?

12
00:01:28,151 --> 00:01:30,445
How about Thursday afternoon?

13
00:01:31,029 --> 00:01:32,780
Okay, 5:00 p.m. is available.

14
00:01:32,864 --> 00:01:34,198
Let's go with that.

15
00:01:34,282 --> 00:01:38,077
Understood, I will book you in
for the 23rd at 5:00 p.m.

16
00:01:38,161 --> 00:01:39,871
-Oh, not on the 23rd.
-What?

17
00:01:41,039 --> 00:01:45,084
I see. Our other available times are--

18
00:01:45,168 --> 00:01:45,960
Midori.

19
00:01:47,962 --> 00:01:49,797
Please excuse me for a moment.

20
00:01:51,049 --> 00:01:54,093
Did we have an appointment
for Ms. Yamada today?

21
00:01:54,177 --> 00:01:55,136
What?

22
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:56,262
Ms. Yamada?

23
00:01:56,346 --> 00:01:57,847
Did you double-book?

24
00:01:57,931 --> 00:01:59,307
She's here right now,

25
00:01:59,390 --> 00:02:02,977
but the doctor is performing
a procedure on another patient.

26
00:02:03,061 --> 00:02:04,020
What?

27
00:02:08,650 --> 00:02:10,151
Excuse me.

28
00:02:11,069 --> 00:02:14,656
I'm very sorry.
I will go check on this right away.

29
00:02:17,408 --> 00:02:19,369
Hello, this is Lachulia Beauty Clinic.

30
00:02:19,452 --> 00:02:21,955
<i>I'm sorry,</i>
<i>I can't make my appointment today.</i>

31
00:02:22,038 --> 00:02:24,791
-Oh, yes… Well…
<i>-Can I reschedule it to tomorrow?</i>

32
00:02:24,874 --> 00:02:27,627
May I have your name
and appointment time--

33
00:02:27,710 --> 00:02:28,670
Excuse me.

34
00:02:28,753 --> 00:02:30,463
-Yes?
-Take my appointment first.

35
00:02:30,546 --> 00:02:33,341
-Yes, please hold on for just a moment.
-When are you open?

36
00:02:33,424 --> 00:02:34,717
-Excuse me!
-Yes?

37
00:02:35,718 --> 00:02:37,512
Well, let's see…

38
00:02:37,595 --> 00:02:39,889
-Is Wednesday at 6:00 p.m. available?
-Wednesday?

39
00:02:39,973 --> 00:02:41,307
Please hold on a moment.

40
00:02:41,391 --> 00:02:42,392
I'm very sorry.

41
00:02:42,475 --> 00:02:44,143
-Midori.
-It's the only day that works.

42
00:02:44,227 --> 00:02:45,270
Yes, I understand.

43
00:02:45,353 --> 00:02:47,105
-6:00 p.m.
-Wednesday?

44
00:02:47,188 --> 00:02:48,231
-Let's see…
-Midori.

45
00:02:48,314 --> 00:02:49,357
Yes!

46
00:02:49,440 --> 00:02:51,192
-Oh…
-Can I get the appointment?

47
00:02:51,275 --> 00:02:52,360
-I understand.
-Midori.

48
00:02:52,443 --> 00:02:53,569
Yes…

49
00:03:00,243 --> 00:03:02,537
RAPID INCREASE
IN FOREIGN TOURISTS IN JAPAN!

50
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:04,622
It's the same thing, every day,

51
00:03:05,289 --> 00:03:08,126
constant appointment changes
and last-minute cancellations.

52
00:03:08,209 --> 00:03:10,128
I feel like I'm going crazy!

53
00:03:12,046 --> 00:03:14,424
Midori! Change the channel.

54
00:03:14,507 --> 00:03:15,800
Our clinic is on.

55
00:03:17,301 --> 00:03:18,594
<i>The case of</i>

56
00:03:18,678 --> 00:03:21,681
<i>Dr. Mieko Matsukawa, the director</i>
<i>of Lachulia Beauty Clinic in Shinjuku,</i>

57
00:03:21,764 --> 00:03:23,099
<i>has been sent to prosecutors.</i>

58
00:03:23,182 --> 00:03:24,809
-What?
<i>-According to the police…</i>

59
00:03:24,892 --> 00:03:26,060
The director?

60
00:03:26,144 --> 00:03:27,311
What? Why?

61
00:03:27,395 --> 00:03:28,813
<i>…provided cosmetic treatments</i>

62
00:03:28,896 --> 00:03:31,482
<i>by using unapproved drugs</i>
<i>and surgical methods on patients.</i>

63
00:03:31,566 --> 00:03:33,276
<i>An order to suspend operations…</i>

64
00:03:33,359 --> 00:03:35,153
An order to suspend operations?

65
00:03:35,236 --> 00:03:38,614
Wait, what's going to happen
to our clinic?

66
00:03:39,115 --> 00:03:43,161
<i>Several clients have spoken out</i>
<i>on social media</i>

67
00:03:43,244 --> 00:03:44,787
<i>about receiving surgery</i>…

68
00:03:44,871 --> 00:03:46,039
Konta?

69
00:03:46,122 --> 00:03:47,123
KONTA

70
00:03:47,790 --> 00:03:48,833
Hello?

71
00:03:48,916 --> 00:03:51,794
<i>Hey, Midori. I'm about to shoot a drama.</i>

72
00:03:51,878 --> 00:03:54,005
<i>This is my dressing room!</i>

73
00:03:54,088 --> 00:03:55,506
Hey, Konta, things are bad.

74
00:03:55,590 --> 00:03:58,593
The clinic I work at might go under.

75
00:03:58,676 --> 00:04:00,762
I might end up unemployed.

76
00:04:01,346 --> 00:04:05,099
<i>Whoa, that's great news, Midori!</i>

77
00:04:05,183 --> 00:04:07,560
<i>You've been saying</i>
<i>you want to quit your job forever!</i>

78
00:04:07,643 --> 00:04:10,605
<i>Well, that's true, but…</i>

79
00:04:10,688 --> 00:04:11,856
Oh, Konta.

80
00:04:11,939 --> 00:04:14,317
Oh, Mr. Jin, hello!

81
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:15,360
JIN ICHIJO

82
00:04:15,443 --> 00:04:17,737
So? Are you in this drama?

83
00:04:17,820 --> 00:04:18,780
Any lines?

84
00:04:18,863 --> 00:04:21,616
I'm just a background patient today.

85
00:04:22,325 --> 00:04:24,535
Oh, you're an extra?

86
00:04:25,244 --> 00:04:26,788
-Hang in there.
-Thank you.

87
00:04:27,872 --> 00:04:29,540
I look forward to working with you!

88
00:04:29,624 --> 00:04:30,458
Thanks.

89
00:04:30,541 --> 00:04:31,584
Thank you.

90
00:04:32,752 --> 00:04:34,170
JIN ICHIJO

91
00:04:35,713 --> 00:04:37,215
KONTA HOSHINO

92
00:04:37,298 --> 00:04:38,549
Sorry about that.

93
00:04:38,633 --> 00:04:42,470
Mr. Jin, the lead actor, just came by,
so we were discussing work.

94
00:04:43,054 --> 00:04:46,933
<i>So then, doesn't that mean you can</i>
<i>take a break for a while?</i>

95
00:04:47,016 --> 00:04:49,811
Well, instead of a while,
it might be forever.

96
00:04:50,478 --> 00:04:53,398
Then you can go you know where.

97
00:04:53,481 --> 00:04:55,149
Grandma's villa!

98
00:04:55,775 --> 00:04:56,692
Oh…

99
00:04:57,360 --> 00:04:58,403
You're right.

100
00:05:04,075 --> 00:05:05,743
THREE DAYS LATER

101
00:05:12,667 --> 00:05:14,585
All right! Cleaning supplies, check!

102
00:05:14,669 --> 00:05:17,004
Change of clothes, check!
Toilet paper, check!

103
00:05:17,088 --> 00:05:18,131
Towels, check!

104
00:05:18,214 --> 00:05:20,967
Meat, check! Snacks, check!
Alcohol, check!

105
00:05:21,050 --> 00:05:22,593
Shall we go then?

106
00:05:23,094 --> 00:05:24,387
On our…

107
00:05:24,470 --> 00:05:26,305
Vacation!

108
00:05:28,891 --> 00:05:30,560
What? Yeah, it's this way.

109
00:05:38,568 --> 00:05:40,278
This feels great.

110
00:05:41,070 --> 00:05:42,321
This is too much walking!

111
00:05:42,405 --> 00:05:44,490
-It's a seagull!
-A seagull!

112
00:05:44,574 --> 00:05:46,868
Oh, someone is fishing!

113
00:05:46,951 --> 00:05:48,953
Are you catching anything?

114
00:05:49,036 --> 00:05:51,038
Hey, stop it, that's embarrassing.

115
00:05:51,122 --> 00:05:52,206
What are you doing?

116
00:05:52,290 --> 00:05:54,417
The villa is that way. Let's go.

117
00:05:56,335 --> 00:05:58,504
Oh, wait! It says "Villa Grounds"!

118
00:05:58,588 --> 00:06:00,339
You're right! Then it's this way.

119
00:06:00,423 --> 00:06:01,465
Yeah.

120
00:06:02,341 --> 00:06:03,718
Whoa.

121
00:06:05,136 --> 00:06:06,470
Hello.

122
00:06:07,471 --> 00:06:09,015
Hello.

123
00:06:09,599 --> 00:06:10,808
Hey.

124
00:06:13,603 --> 00:06:15,271
Chainsaw Woman?

125
00:06:16,355 --> 00:06:17,899
What's that?

126
00:06:17,982 --> 00:06:21,485
A woman who is a Chainsaw Man,
therefore Chainsaw Woman?

127
00:06:21,569 --> 00:06:24,614
So that's a Chainsaw Woman?

128
00:06:24,697 --> 00:06:26,949
-Are you a Chainsaw Woman?
-Be quiet!

129
00:06:27,783 --> 00:06:29,869
This is tough! So tough!

130
00:06:29,952 --> 00:06:32,163
Hey, what are you doing?

131
00:06:33,039 --> 00:06:35,124
Konta, look! The ocean!

132
00:06:36,042 --> 00:06:37,585
Wow, it's so close!

133
00:06:37,668 --> 00:06:39,503
-It's a slope, it's dangerous!
-Watch out!

134
00:06:39,587 --> 00:06:42,298
Konta, be careful!

135
00:06:42,381 --> 00:06:43,716
You got it?

136
00:06:43,799 --> 00:06:45,801
-I got it open.
-I'll take it.

137
00:06:50,223 --> 00:06:52,808
-We made it!
-Awesome!

138
00:06:52,892 --> 00:06:56,229
Are you catching anything?

139
00:06:56,312 --> 00:06:57,521
He can't hear you.

140
00:06:58,898 --> 00:07:00,441
Let's take a picture.

141
00:07:00,524 --> 00:07:01,692
Yeah, let's do it!

142
00:07:01,776 --> 00:07:02,944
Okay, here we go.

143
00:07:03,027 --> 00:07:04,737
-Okay!
-Say cheese!

144
00:07:04,820 --> 00:07:05,821
Yay!

145
00:07:05,905 --> 00:07:06,948
All right.

146
00:07:08,282 --> 00:07:11,160
-Wow, awesome!
-It's huge!

147
00:07:14,872 --> 00:07:16,749
The kitchen is amazing too!

148
00:07:18,084 --> 00:07:19,961
-What?
-The sofa is giant!

149
00:07:20,962 --> 00:07:22,421
So fluffy!

150
00:07:22,922 --> 00:07:24,382
This is insane!

151
00:07:24,465 --> 00:07:27,677
To think this view is all ours.

152
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:30,429
That's right, it belongs to us,
brother and sister!

153
00:07:30,513 --> 00:07:32,431
Forward roll on the sofa!

154
00:07:39,855 --> 00:07:42,233
I heard that after Grandma
divorced Grandpa,

155
00:07:42,316 --> 00:07:44,610
she became estranged
from our Hoshino family,

156
00:07:44,694 --> 00:07:48,114
but she remarried a really
wealthy man and built this villa.

157
00:07:48,197 --> 00:07:49,865
Grandma was amazing!

158
00:07:49,949 --> 00:07:50,783
That's right.

159
00:07:50,866 --> 00:07:52,577
And since Grandma passed away,

160
00:07:52,660 --> 00:07:55,955
the relatives on that side
haven't been using it lately,

161
00:07:56,038 --> 00:07:58,332
so we get to use it!

162
00:07:58,416 --> 00:07:59,792
Yay!

163
00:08:03,671 --> 00:08:05,715
Hey! Look at that.

164
00:08:06,299 --> 00:08:07,216
Look!

165
00:08:09,468 --> 00:08:10,928
It's really something.

166
00:08:12,930 --> 00:08:14,140
-Let's go?
-Yes.

167
00:08:14,223 --> 00:08:15,224
Come on!

168
00:08:16,142 --> 00:08:17,184
All right!

169
00:08:17,268 --> 00:08:20,229
-Wow!
-The yard is huge!

170
00:08:21,522 --> 00:08:24,609
Okay, there we go!

171
00:08:24,692 --> 00:08:25,735
All done.

172
00:08:30,823 --> 00:08:32,617
-Amazing!
-It's surprisingly steep!

173
00:08:32,700 --> 00:08:34,869
-Wait up!
-Be careful!

174
00:08:34,952 --> 00:08:37,371
-Come on!
-It's surprisingly steep! Watch out!

175
00:08:37,455 --> 00:08:39,373
Konta, summer oranges!

176
00:08:39,457 --> 00:08:40,625
Awesome!

177
00:08:41,125 --> 00:08:43,169
I wonder if Grandma liked summer oranges.

178
00:08:43,252 --> 00:08:45,129
Wow, there are so many.

179
00:08:45,212 --> 00:08:46,422
Grandma…

180
00:08:47,423 --> 00:08:49,216
If we sold all of these,
how much would we earn?

181
00:08:49,300 --> 00:08:50,217
Konta!

182
00:08:50,301 --> 00:08:52,470
I was just praying to Grandma in heaven!

183
00:08:53,179 --> 00:08:54,055
That's right.

184
00:08:54,138 --> 00:08:56,891
We don't have a Buddhist altar here,
but I should pray.

185
00:08:57,558 --> 00:09:01,270
Thank you, Grandma,
for leaving us such a wonderful villa.

186
00:09:02,980 --> 00:09:05,358
We will take good care of it, Grandma.

187
00:09:05,441 --> 00:09:07,526
Well, want to try one?

188
00:09:07,610 --> 00:09:09,111
-All right.
-Let's!

189
00:09:09,195 --> 00:09:11,322
They're really big. How about that one?

190
00:09:11,405 --> 00:09:12,615
-Should I grab it?
-Yes!

191
00:09:18,788 --> 00:09:20,122
So sour! What is this?

192
00:09:20,206 --> 00:09:23,376
I know. When I cut it open,
it was so sour, I couldn't eat it.

193
00:09:23,459 --> 00:09:25,878
We can't sell these.
They're as sour as lemons.

194
00:09:25,961 --> 00:09:28,005
We can use them
as a substitute for lemons.

195
00:09:28,089 --> 00:09:29,799
For cooking or making sour drinks.

196
00:09:29,882 --> 00:09:32,843
And this leftover thick peel…

197
00:09:35,054 --> 00:09:36,472
can be used for cleaning!

198
00:09:36,555 --> 00:09:38,766
You're so impressive, Midori!

199
00:09:38,849 --> 00:09:40,309
You're good at cleaning and cooking,

200
00:09:40,393 --> 00:09:43,521
and your face is cute like mine,
so why don't you have a boyfriend?

201
00:09:44,105 --> 00:09:45,690
You don't have a girlfriend either.

202
00:09:47,191 --> 00:09:48,150
Well, that's true.

203
00:09:49,402 --> 00:09:52,071
To think we would end up
spending a vacation together

204
00:09:52,154 --> 00:09:54,198
at such a wonderful seaside villa.

205
00:09:54,281 --> 00:09:57,576
It's not really a vacation for you…
Aren't you unemployed?

206
00:09:57,660 --> 00:09:58,869
What?

207
00:09:58,953 --> 00:10:00,621
Stop putting it so unromantically!

208
00:10:00,705 --> 00:10:01,914
My bad, sorry.

209
00:10:11,716 --> 00:10:14,218
Since no one had been here for a while,

210
00:10:14,301 --> 00:10:18,931
I thought it would be more overgrown,
but it's actually pretty well-maintained.

211
00:10:19,598 --> 00:10:20,641
All right…

212
00:10:37,366 --> 00:10:38,492
Hello.

213
00:10:40,244 --> 00:10:42,329
H-Hello.

214
00:10:43,831 --> 00:10:44,874
Who are you?

215
00:10:46,792 --> 00:10:50,838
I'm the granddaughter
of the owner of this villa.

216
00:10:51,505 --> 00:10:53,340
You can call me Hoshino.

217
00:10:54,008 --> 00:10:56,886
This is the villa
of my late grandmother, Nobuko.

218
00:10:57,553 --> 00:11:00,097
Oh, Ms. Nobuko.

219
00:11:06,187 --> 00:11:10,357
Because this villa
is near the ocean, the wind…

220
00:11:12,234 --> 00:11:14,820
can be very strong at times.

221
00:11:16,405 --> 00:11:17,281
Oh.

222
00:11:18,407 --> 00:11:19,283
Got it.

223
00:11:20,326 --> 00:11:21,827
Look, here it is again.

224
00:11:32,463 --> 00:11:34,215
S-So handsome.

225
00:11:35,257 --> 00:11:37,510
Midori! I found a drone beetle!

226
00:11:37,593 --> 00:11:40,012
Vroom! A drone beetle…

227
00:11:40,095 --> 00:11:41,263
Wow, a handsome guy.

228
00:11:43,265 --> 00:11:44,642
Nice to meet you.

229
00:11:44,725 --> 00:11:47,478
I manage these villa grounds.

230
00:11:48,479 --> 00:11:51,273
I'm the caretaker, Nishigami.

231
00:11:51,857 --> 00:11:53,859
Oh, the caretaker.

232
00:11:53,943 --> 00:11:55,444
I see.

233
00:11:55,528 --> 00:11:58,113
So there's someone like that here.
That's convenient.

234
00:11:58,197 --> 00:12:02,076
We haven't been here since we were kids,
so we have no idea how things work.

235
00:12:02,952 --> 00:12:04,995
Oh, this is my brother.

236
00:12:05,079 --> 00:12:06,539
My older brother, Konta.

237
00:12:06,622 --> 00:12:07,581
I'm Konta.

238
00:12:07,665 --> 00:12:08,832
Mr. Konta.

239
00:12:10,125 --> 00:12:11,043
And you are?

240
00:12:12,628 --> 00:12:14,838
Well, I'm Midori.

241
00:12:14,922 --> 00:12:16,757
My name is Midori Hoshino.

242
00:12:18,300 --> 00:12:19,343
Ms. Midori.

243
00:12:19,426 --> 00:12:20,469
Yes.

244
00:12:23,097 --> 00:12:28,102
Are you planning to spend
your time off at this villa?

245
00:12:28,185 --> 00:12:32,439
Yes. They said on TV
that Japanese people aren't good

246
00:12:32,523 --> 00:12:33,899
at taking vacations.

247
00:12:33,983 --> 00:12:35,317
-They did say that.
-Yeah.

248
00:12:35,401 --> 00:12:38,571
So we thought we would try taking
one of those things called a vacation.

249
00:12:38,654 --> 00:12:39,530
That's right.

250
00:12:39,613 --> 00:12:40,614
Yes.

251
00:12:42,283 --> 00:12:43,826
A vacation…

252
00:13:00,718 --> 00:13:02,094
Midori Hoshino.

253
00:13:02,928 --> 00:13:04,263
Konta Hoshino.

254
00:13:22,656 --> 00:13:24,199
<i>Did you call for me?</i>

255
00:13:24,283 --> 00:13:27,036
<i>I am the Grim Reaper</i>
<i>in charge of Tatsumi Town.</i>

256
00:13:27,953 --> 00:13:31,790
<i>Is there anything to report from</i>
<i>the Shiokaze district of Tatsumi Town?</i>

257
00:13:33,042 --> 00:13:35,002
No. Nothing in particular.

258
00:13:36,754 --> 00:13:39,632
<i>Those villa grounds</i>
<i>are under your jurisdiction.</i>

259
00:13:39,715 --> 00:13:41,592
<i>You do know that in one month,</i>

260
00:13:41,675 --> 00:13:46,430
<i>a landslide caused by a massive typhoon</i>
<i>will kill all the residents, correct?</i>

261
00:13:48,641 --> 00:13:49,725
Yes.

262
00:14:00,527 --> 00:14:04,531
Konta! Summer orange juice! Try it!

263
00:14:04,615 --> 00:14:05,991
-What? You made it into juice?
-Yes!

264
00:14:06,075 --> 00:14:07,159
Thanks, Midori.

265
00:14:07,242 --> 00:14:08,952
-You're welcome.
-Down the hatch.

266
00:14:10,245 --> 00:14:11,080
So sour!

267
00:14:11,163 --> 00:14:12,039
Gross!

268
00:14:12,122 --> 00:14:14,375
-It's sour! What is this?
-You fell for it!

269
00:14:14,458 --> 00:14:15,668
Hey, Midori!

270
00:14:15,751 --> 00:14:17,544
Midori, wait up!

271
00:14:17,628 --> 00:14:18,837
Watch out!

272
00:14:18,921 --> 00:14:22,132
-Stay back!
-Here it comes, bam!

273
00:14:23,175 --> 00:14:25,469
-Here I go!
-Come at me!

274
00:14:25,552 --> 00:14:27,763
Are you or are you not?

275
00:14:27,846 --> 00:14:28,847
No!

276
00:14:28,931 --> 00:14:31,850
Hey, this area is mine!

277
00:14:31,934 --> 00:14:33,686
-My area!
-Stop!

278
00:14:33,769 --> 00:14:35,270
This is mine!

279
00:14:53,372 --> 00:14:55,040
Yes?

280
00:14:55,124 --> 00:14:56,500
-We came.
-We came.

281
00:14:57,084 --> 00:15:00,087
Wow! What is this place?
It's absolutely amazing!

282
00:15:00,754 --> 00:15:02,339
<i>This is my friend, Tetsuro.</i>

283
00:15:02,423 --> 00:15:04,591
A barbecue needs a man's strength!

284
00:15:04,675 --> 00:15:05,676
Huh?

285
00:15:05,759 --> 00:15:07,845
More people are here.

286
00:15:07,928 --> 00:15:09,430
<i>Who is this handsome guy?</i>

287
00:15:09,513 --> 00:15:12,141
<i>This is Mr. Nishigami,</i>
<i>who takes care of the villas around here.</i>

288
00:15:14,476 --> 00:15:16,186
Vacations are the best!

289
00:15:16,270 --> 00:15:17,396
The best!

290
00:15:17,980 --> 00:15:20,357
<i>Let's all spend this summer here together!</i>

291
00:15:20,941 --> 00:15:23,736
<i>Until the moment</i>
<i>the flame of their lives goes out,</i>

292
00:15:24,403 --> 00:15:26,864
I will watch over them closely.

293
00:15:28,449 --> 00:15:29,408
Subtitle translation by: Maslin F.

